±saukunis cin shek`mnil o' henris mokle mot`xrobebs rom kit`xulob,ggonia, es ambavi, ager, axla moxda, shens z'alian axlobels an sulac` shen gadagxada t`avs da unebliet` mot`xrobis "mt`avari gmiri xdebi". scored amashia o' henris popularobis saidumlo. gip`ik`rit` ukugardasaxvaze? mashin am saxelcodebis mot`xrobis cakit`xva mogicevt`. siqvaruli miiqvans mouxelt`ebel mz'arc`vels, jimi valentains, im daskvnamde, rom seip`ebis gatexvas unda sheeshvas. bedis dac`invit` ki, scored saqvareli k`alisa da gant`k`muli maz'ebris t`valcin moucevs didi seip`is iz'ulebit` gaxsna masshi shemt`xvevit` ch`aketili patara gogonas gadasarch`enad. seip`ebis gatexvis "didostatma" ic`is, am siket`is sanac`vlod satusag'o elodeba - veravis daumtkic`ebs, rom z'arc`as sheeshva, z'vel c`odvebs ki vin apatiebs. ic`is, magram gogonas mainc` ixsnis.
amis shemdeg mkit`xveli mocme xdeba sruliad moulodnelad dasasrulisa, romelic` qvela shesaz'lo carmodgenas amsxvrevs da siket`is qovlisshemz'leobashi gvarcmunebbs. scored aset`i - didi seket`it`a da siqvarulit` savse mot`xrobebia am krebulshi..."Û
ØBy the author of "Canal Dreams" and "The Wasp Factory", this novel is about three men - Graham Park, Steven Grant and Quiss. No trio of people could be further apart, but their separate courses are set for collision."Û
Øsheron dreiperis "gonebis mig'ma" ambavia patara gogonaze - melodize, romelsac` c`erebruli dambla ak`vs. melodis metqveleba ar sheuz'lia, arada, mas z'alian, z'alian bevri ram ak`vs sat`k`meli... is inkluziur klasshi scavlobs da z'alian xshirad ucevs klaselebis da mascavleblebis mxridan damakninebeli mopqrobis atana. es aris z'alian mamac`i bavshvis sulis shemz'vreli, lamazi da sevdiani istoria, ambavi gogonaze, romelmac` z'alian bevri cinaag'mdegoba gadalaxa da sakut`ar t`avsac` ki ajoba. es spec`ialuri sachiroebebis mk`one bavshvis pirvel pirshi moqolili da sheulamazeblad mot`xrobili ambavia"ê
çiseve rogorc` madat`ovis cina romanebshi, mkit`xveli ak`ac` mraval istoriul, t`u mcerlis p`antaziit` shek`mnil personazhs shexvdeba da carsulis surat`ebsac` gaixsenebs, magram cina cignebisgan gansxvavebit`, es romani ori nacilisgan shedgeba. romanis meore nacilshi mcerali axal realobas k`mnis, romlis p`inalshic` mkit`xveli xvdeba, rom madat`ovis oc`daat`cliani istoria sinamdvileshi virtualuri realoba, oc`dameert`e saukuneshi shek`mnili kompiuteruli t`amashi "mejik` polisi" qop`ila."í
êsagangebo p`ormatis - e. c. jibis cigni, romlis tareba da gac`noba mkit`xvels nebismier adgilas sheuz'lia. gamoch`enili k`art`veli mcerlebis t`valit` danaxuli carsuli - originalurad carmodgenili istoriuli realiebi, literaturul personazhebad gardak`mnili realuri pirovnebebi, mat`i saoc`ari t`avgadasavlebi da mimzidveli siuzhetebi, rac` gulgrils aravis datovebs."ò
ï"A triumph of love & art."--The Washington Post
In a small Pennsylvania town in the late 1940s, schoolteacher George Caldwell yearns to find some meaning in his life. Alone with his teenage son for three days in a blizzard, Caldwell sees his son grow & change as he himself begins to lose touch with his life. Interwoven with the myth of Chiron, the noblest centaur, & his relationship to the Titan Prometheus, "The Centaur" is one of Updike's most brilliant novels.--From the Paperback edition."ò
ïema vudhauzi lamazi, chkviani da mdidari axalgazrda k`ali iqo, ket`ilmocqobili saxlisa da xalisiani gunebis patroni. masshi t`it`k`os t`avi moeqara qop`ierebis siket`eebs da lamis ukve oc`daert`i celi amk`veqnad ise gaetarebina, rom tkivilisa da dardis shesaxeb prak`tikulad arap`eri ic`oda.
emas mamas - z'aliam mosiqvarule, t`vinier kac`s - ori k`alishvili hqavda. debs shoris umc`rosi ema gaxldat`, romelic` up`rosi dis gat`xovebis shemdeg mamiseul saxlshi adreuli asakidanve diasaxlisobda. deda imdeni xnis cin gardasc`vloda, rom emas misi alersi bundovnad t`u axsovda, misi adgili ki ag'mzrdels daekavebina - arach`veulebriv k`als, romlis mzrunveloba da sit`bo dedobrivs arap`rit` ch`amouvardeboda.
mis teilors mister vudhauzis saxlshi c`xovrebis t`ek`vsmetcliani stazhi hk`onda da up`ro megobari et`k`moda, vidre ag'mzrdeli. mas vudhauzis orive k`alishvili uqvarda, magram ema - gamorch`eulad. am oris siaxlove debisas arap`rit` ch`amouvardeboda. jer kidev mashin, sanam ,,ag'mzrdeli" erk`va, mis teilors t`avisi damqoli buneba ar az'levda simkac`ris sashualebas; mas mere ki, rac` avtoritetis isedac` mkrt`ali konturebi carsuls ch`ahbarda, is da ema ert`guli megobrebivit` c`xovrobdnen da ormxrivi grz'nobebi akavshirebdat`. ema mis teilors azrs did pativs sc`emda, magram sakut`ar c`xovrebas t`avisi shexedulebisamebr ganagebda; qovelt`vis imas aket`ebda, rac` moeprianeboda da mis mdgomareobit` gamocveuli sap`rt`xec` scored ak` imaleboda: mas hk`onda absoluturi z'alaup`leba da sachiroze uket`esi carmodgena sakut`ar t`avze, amitom mxolod t`avis chkuaze dadioda. es arasaxarbielo garemoeba mis araert` c`xovrebiseul siames emuk`reboda gaup`erulebit`, t`umc`a sap`rt`xe jerjerobit` imdenad sheumch`neveli iqo, rom emast`vis ubedurebis cqaros odnavac` ar carmoadgenda"ô
ñot`ar chilaz'is t`xzulebebis at`tomeuli, mesame tomi. romanshi "rkinis t`eatri", carmodgenilia me-19 saukunis dasasrulis da me-20 saukunis dasacqisis k`art`uli c`xovrebis p`art`o panorama. 1983 cels es romani rust`avelis premiit` ag'inishna."õ
òOnce, on a winter's night many years ago, after a heavy snow, the devil passed through the Scottish fishing town of Coldhaven, leaving a trail of dark hoofprints across the streets and roofs of the sleeping town.
Michael Gardiner has lived in Coldhaven all his life, but still feels like an outsider, a blow-in. When Moira Birnie decides that her abusive husband is the devil and then kills herself and her two young sons, a terrible chain of events begins. Michael's infatuation with Moira's teenage daughter takes him on a journey towards a defined fate, where he is forced to face his present and then, finally, his past..."ö
óSergei Diaghilev and his extraordinary Ballets Russes revolutionized ballet for all time. From 1909 to 1929, the Ballets Russes attracted avant-garde composers such as Stravinsky, dancers such as Nijinsky and Massine, and designers such as Bakst, Goncharova, Picasso, Matisse, and Chanel, and even a very young George Balanchine, all of whom helped to create true collaborations never before seen in the performing arts. Now, this major book, published to accompany an exhibition that originated at the V&A and is now traveling to the National Gallery of Art, Washington, examines the origins, development, and long-term influence of the Ballets Russes, complete with costumes, sets, and performance photographs. This beautiful book showcases artistic collaboration at its finest.
"This fascinating book should be on every ballet lovers' gift list."
--Suzy Menkes, The New York Times"ø
õcignshi ag'cerili garemo da movlenebi avtoris piradi gamoc`dilebis anareklia, rac` kidev up`ro amz'ap`rebs romanisadmi interess. begbederi c`inikurad ag'cers im gamoch`enil adamiant`a zg'vargadasul simdidres, romelt`ac` ket`ildg'eoba danarch`eni msop`lios ubedurebisa da sulieri gag'atakebis xarjze moipoves. msop`lioshi qvelap`eri elvisuscrap`esad ic`vleba. mag'ali tek`nologiebis mig'cevebs sazg'vari ara ak`vs, magram veranairi tek`nikuri progresi ver shec`vlis adamianur grz'nobebs. adamians dg'esac` isev ise uqvars, sz'uls, stkiva, eshinia, dardobs...mkit`xvels ut`uod sheac`bunebs cignshi ag'cerili axamsi sc`enebi. es chaobi auc`ilebeli gaxda imist`vis, rom ok`tav parango sulierad ganicmindos...shez'lebs ki amas? es mkit`xvelma unda gadacqvitos..."	
